-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/720b46cc-a816-4c43-a29e-942f3a39b6e2
-- title:
--   Geometric step-size draws, $p_0=1/\log(T+10)$ and the step sizes $\eta_i^t$ of MA-AdaOGD
-- statement:
--   A random variable $Y$ is **Geometric($p$) on $\{1,2,\dots\}$** if it is measurable and
--   $$
--   \mathbb P(Y=k)=(1-p)^{k-1}p\quad(k\in\{1,2,\dots\}),\qquad \mathbb P(Y=0)=0 .
--   $$
--   Algorithm 3 (MA-AdaOGD) with horizon $T$ uses $p_0=1/\log(T+10)$ and draws, for every agent $i\in\{1,\dots,N\}$ and round $t\in\{1,\dots,T\}$, a variable $M_i^t\sim\mathrm{Geometric}(p_0)$; the family $\{M_i^t\}_{1\le i\le N,1\le t\le T}$ is independent. Its step sizes are
--   $$
--   \eta_i^{t+1}=\frac{t+1}{\sqrt{1+\max\{M_i^1,\dots,M_i^t\}}},\qquad \eta_i^1=1 .
--   $$
--   We also write $\max\{M_i^1,\dots,M_i^t\}$ for the running maximum, $\max_{1\le i\le N,1\le t\le T}M_i^t$ for the overall maximum, and $\sigma(\{\eta_i^t\}_{1\le i\le N,1\le t\le T})$ for the σ-algebra generated by the step sizes, which is the conditioning σ-algebra of Lemma 3.10.
--
--   The randomized step size is what makes the algorithm adaptive: it needs no knowledge of the strong monotonicity modulus $\beta$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The law is written on $\{1,2,\dots\}$ directly; Mathlib's `geometricPMFReal` (support $\{0,1,\dots\}$) is not used. `M i t` is agent $i$'s draw at round $t$ (rounds start at $1$); the i.i.d. family is indexed by `Fin N × Fin T` as `M i (s+1)`. The paper never defines $\eta_i^1$; the empty maximum is $0$, so the formula gives $\eta_i^1=1$.
-- source:
--   Jordan, Lin & Zhou, Adaptive, Doubly Optimal No-Regret Learning in Strongly Monotone and Exp-Concave Games with Gradient Feedback, arXiv:2310.14085v4, §2.1, p.8 (Geometric($p_0$)); Algorithm 3, lines 2, 5, 6, p.15; Lemma 3.10, p.16 (conditioning on $\{\eta_i^t\}$)

import Mathlib

namespace AdaOGD

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory

/-- `Y ∼ Geometric(p)` on `{1, 2, …}`: `ℙ(Y = k) = (1 − p)^{k−1} p` for `k ∈ {1, 2, …}`
(Jordan, Lin & Zhou, Adaptive, Doubly Optimal No-Regret Learning…, arXiv:2310.14085v4, §2.1, p.8).

**Formalization Note** The support is `{1, 2, …}`, so `ℙ(Y = 0) = 0` is part of the law; Mathlib's
`geometricPMFReal` is the law on `{0, 1, …}` and is not used. `Y` is measurable. -/
def IsGeometric {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (P : Measure Ω) (p : ℝ) (Y : Ω → ℕ) : Prop :=
  Measurable Y ∧ P.real {ω | Y ω = 0} = 0 ∧
    ∀ k : ℕ, 1 ≤ k → P.real {ω | Y ω = k} = (1 - p) ^ (k - 1) * p

/-- The parameter `p₀ = 1/log(T + 10)` of Algorithm 3, line 2 (arXiv:2310.14085v4, p.15). -/
noncomputable def p0 (T : ℕ) : ℝ := 1 / Real.log ((T : ℝ) + 10)

/-- The step-size draws of Algorithm 3 (arXiv:2310.14085v4, p.15, lines 2 and 5, and "We again
choose independently identical distributed geometric random variables, i.e., Mᵗᵢ ∼ Geometric(p₀)"):
the family `{Mᵗᵢ : 1 ≤ i ≤ N, 1 ≤ t ≤ T}` is i.i.d. Geometric(`p₀`) on `{1, 2, …}` with
`p₀ = 1/log(T + 10)`.

**Formalization Note** `M i t` is agent `i`'s draw at round `t`; rounds start at `1`, and the
family indexed by `(i, s) ∈ Fin N × Fin T` is `M i (s + 1)`. Values of `M i t` for `t = 0` or
`t > T` are unconstrained and never used. -/
def IsGeomDraws {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (P : Measure Ω) {N : ℕ} (T : ℕ)
    (M : Fin N → ℕ → Ω → ℕ) : Prop :=
  iIndepFun (fun p : Fin N × Fin T => M p.1 ((p.2 : ℕ) + 1)) P ∧
    ∀ i : Fin N, ∀ t : ℕ, 1 ≤ t → t ≤ T → IsGeometric P (p0 T) (M i t)

/-- The running maximum `max{M¹ᵢ, …, Mᵗᵢ}` of agent `i`'s draws (arXiv:2310.14085v4, Algorithm 3,
line 6, p.15); it is `0` for `t = 0` (empty maximum). -/
def runMax {Ω : Type*} {N : ℕ} (M : Fin N → ℕ → Ω → ℕ) (i : Fin N) (t : ℕ) (ω : Ω) : ℕ :=
  (Finset.Icc 1 t).sup fun s => M i s ω

/-- The overall maximum `max_{1≤i≤N, 1≤t≤T} Mᵗᵢ` (arXiv:2310.14085v4, (3.3)–(3.6), pp.17–18). -/
def maxDraw {Ω : Type*} {N : ℕ} (M : Fin N → ℕ → Ω → ℕ) (T : ℕ) (ω : Ω) : ℕ :=
  (Finset.univ ×ˢ Finset.Icc 1 T).sup fun p : Fin N × ℕ => M p.1 p.2 ω

/-- The adaptive step size of Algorithm 3, line 6 (arXiv:2310.14085v4, p.15):
`ηᵗ⁺¹ᵢ = (t + 1)/√(1 + max{M¹ᵢ, …, Mᵗᵢ})`, i.e. `ηᵗᵢ = t/√(1 + max{M¹ᵢ, …, Mᵗ⁻¹ᵢ})`.

**Formalization Note** The paper never defines `η¹ᵢ`; here the empty maximum is `0`, so
`η¹ᵢ = 1/√1 = 1`. The value at `t = 0` is `0` and is never used. -/
noncomputable def eta {Ω : Type*} {N : ℕ} (M : Fin N → ℕ → Ω → ℕ) (i : Fin N) (t : ℕ) (ω : Ω) :
    ℝ :=
  (t : ℝ) / Real.sqrt (1 + (runMax M i (t - 1) ω : ℝ))

/-- The σ-algebra generated by the step sizes `{ηᵗᵢ}_{1≤i≤N, 1≤t≤T}`, the conditioning σ-algebra of
Lemma 3.10 (arXiv:2310.14085v4, p.16). -/
@[reducible] noncomputable def etaSigma {Ω : Type*} {N : ℕ} (M : Fin N → ℕ → Ω → ℕ) (T : ℕ) : MeasurableSpace Ω :=
  ⨆ i : Fin N, ⨆ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T, MeasurableSpace.comap (eta M i t) inferInstance

end AdaOGD


